-- title:
--   Original stopped Gaussian G/H L1 source and positive Brownian tube refute fixed-band cash upper almost everywhere
-- statement:
--   For the original full stopped physical-grid Gaussian G/H martingale source with integrable restricted L1 limit, if the discounted centred source is controlled by a positive-measure Brownian event and its eventual mesh values are uniformly bounded by epsilon<=1/4000, the original cash upper fails almost everywhere on that event. B159 supplies the a.e source-noise bound; B170 combines it with the Proved strict Stieltjes cash counterexample B166 and positive event measure. This is a direct conditional no-go certificate for the original B52p assertion; native tube positivity and original global source convergence remain to be instantiated.

